  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the subject of the meme",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Anthony T.I. Thornton, as the meme's humor and intent are directed at him. The textual elements ('unnecessary life-vest', 'ice cubes float') are used to create a false equivalence that implies the subject is overprepared or unnecessary, thereby projecting the user's interpretation of the joke onto his visual representation. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the implied audience (the user) is positioned as the one interpreting the joke and applying the analogy to the subject.",
